A method that contains a P/Invoke saved every callee-saved register in its prolog (s1..s11, so a GC
stack walk could find them while the thread is in native code) and was forced to keep a frame pointer
(the P/Invoke frame setup needs one). perf-27 removed the P/Invoke transition itself on riscv64 - the
zkVM guest has no GC stack walk and no thread suspension - but left both rules in place. On the
Nethermind guest the cost sits in the precompile wrappers: SpanHelpers.MemmoveNative (47k calls per
block) spent 26 of its 35 executed instructions on saving and restoring 13 registers, 1.2M steps
(0.9%) on block 25532480; ZeroMemoryNative likewise. Both rules are now skipped on riscv64, so these
methods get the ordinary prolog (only the registers they modify, frameless when nothing else needs FP).

RISC-V64 zkVM: P/Invoke methods no longer save all callee-saved registers nor force a frame pointer.

diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/codegencommon.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/codegencommon.cpp
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/codegencommon.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/codegencommon.cpp
@@ -5074,11 +5074,17 @@ void CodeGen::genFinalizeFrame()
     }
 
     /* If we have any pinvoke calls, we might potentially trash everything */
+#if !defined(TARGET_RISCV64)
+    // RISC-V zkVM: the P/Invoke transition is not emitted (perf-27), there is no GC stack walk
+    // that would need every callee-saved register on the frame, and the frame pointer is not
+    // forced for these methods (fgMorph). Saving s1..s11 around a two-instruction precompile
+    // wrapper (SpanHelpers.MemmoveNative: 26 of its 35 steps) is pure overhead there.
     if (m_compiler->compMethodRequiresPInvokeFrame())
     {
         noway_assert(isFramePointerUsed()); // Setup of Pinvoke frame currently requires an EBP style frame
         regSet.rsSetRegsModified(RBM_INT_CALLEE_SAVED & ~RBM_FPBASE);
     }
+#endif // !TARGET_RISCV64
 
     // Parameter homing may need an additional register to handle conflicts if
     // all callee trash registers are used by parameters.
diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/morph.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/morph.cpp
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/morph.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/morph.cpp
@@ -15311,10 +15311,13 @@ void Compiler::fgSetOptions()
 #endif // TARGET_X86
     }
 
+#if !defined(TARGET_RISCV64)
+    // RISC-V zkVM: no P/Invoke frame is set up (perf-27), so no frame pointer is needed for it.
     if (compMethodRequiresPInvokeFrame())
     {
         codeGen->setFramePointerRequired(true); // Setup of Pinvoke frame currently requires an EBP style frame
     }
+#endif // !TARGET_RISCV64
 
     if (info.compPublishStubParam)
     {
